    {
      "id": "c491d212-776f-5042-bcda-3948d2729a2f",
      "name": "Overview and requirements",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nTeams that need document-arrival notices in a designated Microsoft Teams channel. Read new Folderit document details, optionally filter an exact folder, post a concise notice, and remember each confirmed event/destination pair. Completed receipts suppress repeats. An uncertain destination result stops processing and holds the lock for manual recovery.\n\n### Setup\nRequires Folderit **Tailor with API access**, a dedicated test destination and provider credentials. Install Folderit using the connection guide below. Tested on n8n **2.46.0** with **n8n-nodes-folderit 0.4.0**; Data Table v1.1 is required.\n\n1. Keep inactive. Choose a stable table name in **Ledger setup settings** and run only **1. Set up receipt table**, once at a time in the same n8n project.\n2. Select the SAME **Folderit OAuth2 API** credential in the Folderit trigger and details action. Set the same account UID in the trigger and **Settings**, plus the teamId and channelId. Select **Microsoft Teams OAuth2** in **Send Teams notification**; use a delegated Microsoft account allowed to post in the target channel. Paste the setup branch's ledgerTableId into Settings. Never put secrets in Settings. Copies processing the same input must share the table.\n3. Activate, allow the first poll, then upload a test file. Inspect the actual channel notice and repeat suppression. Manual previews can include historical events and send notices.\n\n### Customization\nSet folderUid for one exact parent, excluding descendants; blank accepts account events. Poll at least hourly. Interruptions beyond 23 hours need reconciliation.\n\n[Connection and first-run guide](https://www.folderit.com/knowledge-base/connect-folderit-to-n8n/) · [Recovery instructions](https://github.com/folderit-dms/n8n-nodes-folderit/blob/main/CUSTOMER-WORKFLOWS.md#recovery-inspect-before-retrying)\n\n[Workflow image](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folderit-dms/n8n-nodes-folderit/main/templates/assets/notify-teams-on-new-documents.png)",
        "width": 860,
        "height": 900,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "77c4431f-3d9a-55ba-956d-ef7add636c90",
      "name": "Intake and selection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · Read new document events\nUse the same account UID and Folderit credential in the trigger and Settings. Read accessible document details and apply the optional exact-folder filter. A missing document stops for inspection.",
        "width": 1080,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "16ac35a0-a13a-5989-a5eb-1541aa9c816c",
      "name": "Serialize processing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1000,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · Process one item at a time\nA shared lock serializes overlapping runs. Confirm ownership before continuing; competing runs wait for about one minute, then stop. There is no automatic lock expiry: a failed run needs inspection.",
        "width": 1280,
        "height": 1080,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b91124f2-fa31-57de-b3b0-064b796ba439",
      "name": "Check saved receipts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2300,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 · Skip confirmed work\nLook up the item’s durable receipt. Completed work follows the upper bypass; a new item continues to the destination action. Pending or inconsistent receipts stop for recovery instead of repeating an uncertain action.",
        "width": 880,
        "height": 1080,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "67b5ae9f-8e07-5e47-8a4a-11762824dc49",
      "name": "Record before writing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3200,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 · Record before notifying\nSave a pending receipt before posting to Teams. Use a delegated work account that can post in the configured channel. A failed or uncertain response holds the lock; inspect the channel before retrying.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9d87f934-171e-54df-8238-0cdcecbedf61",
      "name": "Verify the destination",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4100,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6 · Check the returned message\nRequire a message ID from Teams before completing the receipt. During acceptance testing, also open the actual channel and check its body and destination; a green execution alone is insufficient.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b8a668e-12cb-58fc-8d99-8a443a7c31a0",
      "name": "Complete and release",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4800,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 7 · Save the result, then unlock\nConfirm the completed receipt before freeing the lock and taking the next item. Retain completed receipts. After a failure, confirm the old owner has stopped and reconcile every pending result before releasing its lock.",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "82027152-0f17-541a-80a1-a4fa6204e56b",
      "name": "Manual receipt-table setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        1080
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · Run setup before the service trigger\nChoose a stable table name, then run this manual branch once. It validates or creates local receipts and the lock without contacting providers. Copy the final ledgerTableId into the main Settings node; preserve this table on upgrades.",
        "width": 2160,
        "height": 650,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
